# `takex` -- the OWNED return that pins its non-owned sources.
#
# `take` returns an owned value and pins nothing; `borrow`/`view` return a
# reference and pin the source for the binding's life. Neither says what four
# stdlib constructors need: `BufWriter.create to: Writer.lock out this` hands
# back an OWNED value whose `sink` field is a reference INTO the argument, so
# the argument has to stay pinned for as long as the result lives. `.lock` is
# the only marker that expresses that today, which is why it cannot retire
# without this one.
#
# This fixture covers the marker itself: it parses, it records as OWNED (so the
# result carries a destructor -- the corpus leak pass is what checks that, not
# the printed line), and it survives the round trip. The PIN is a separate rule
# and gets its own fixture.
#
# At the parent commit `.takex` is not a marker at all and the emitter refuses
# the binding with E0500.
Src: class {
    label: String
}

W: class {
    label: String
}

mk: function {from: Src.borrow} out W.takex is {
    return (W label: from.label.copy)
}

main: function is {
    a: Src label: "source".string
    w: mk from: a
    print "takex result: \{w.label}"
    # the source is untouched and still owns its own String
    print "source intact: \{a.label}"
}
